In article <C5t8v0.HzH@ucdavis.edu> zerkle@cs.ucdavis.edu (Dan Zerkle) writes:

>Demigods should be scary!  If there are any artifacts left in the
>game, give them to the demigods!  After all, they needed to pick up
>the things to ascend themselves, right?  Why shouldn't they still have
>them?
>
>Start with the really nasty artifacts:  Excalibur, Stormbringer,
>Vorpal Blade, the Tsurugi of Muramasa, Magicbane and Grayswandir.
^^^^^^^^^^^^^  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
>Make sure they're all enchanted to +4 or +5.  After that, go with
>the artifacts people can be resistant to:  Frost/Fire Brand and
>Mjollnir.  Then go with Snickersnee and Cleaver.
>Finally, if there are any weaponless demigods left, go with
>the artifacts for "other" monsters, like Ogresmasher, Giantslayer, and
>so on.

The demigods already get some artifacts, I believe; when trying out Astral
Plane in Wizard mode, I encountered one wielding Firebrand.

Still, it can be pretty dangerous.  Do you really want:

Minamoto Yoritomo swings his tsurugi named Tsurugi of Muramasa! -more-
Minamoto Yoritomo cuts deeply into your flesh! -more-
You die... -more-

?  I think it can be a bit unfair to the player.

>Of course, they should _all_ be wearing amulets of lifesaving.

I agree with this one.
>
>This would not be unbalancing.  By this point in the game, characters
>should have everything they need.  Giving them the extra equipment
>won't help, but will just add weight.  The nasty effects of the Vorpal
>Blade and the Tsuguri could be avoided by using an amulet of
>lifesaving or two (one guaranteed in Vlad's tower, remember?).

But the demigods, with the help of the angels and priests, are way more
numerous.  I would agree with your idea if the demigod (singular) is the only
monster on the level whom you have to defeat before you can sacrifice the
Amulet.  Imagine a demigod wizard using Magicbane to purge you (getting rid of
*all* your intrinsics)...

>To make killing the demigods worthwhile, they should each carry six
>or seven gems, all valuable (no glass).  Gems are the only thing in the
>game an ascending character _really_ wants.

I doubt that such kinds of demigods are killable, particularly because they
have those angels to help them.  Of course, if you get a horde of angels as
pets (which would be balancing but hard to play), then it may not be that
unbalancing.  Still...

